assertion  XBD.pthread.h.009
anchor     basedefs/pthread.h.html#DESCRIPTION/PTHREAD_PRIO_NONE
class      conditional
when       TPP|TPI|RPP|RPI
since      2001
says       PTHREAD_PRIO_NONE, PTHREAD_PRIO_INHERIT and
           PTHREAD_PRIO_PROTECT, as far as defined, have different
           values.
note       Alternatives that a get function must report apart (Q-165).
test       t/009-prio-protocol.c
nomutant   header content check; needs the Tier 0 header mutants

assertion  XBD.pthread.h.010
anchor     basedefs/pthread.h.html#DESCRIPTION/PTHREAD_MUTEX_INITIALIZER
class      required
since      2001
says       PTHREAD_MUTEX_INITIALIZER, PTHREAD_COND_INITIALIZER and
           PTHREAD_RWLOCK_INITIALIZER initialise static objects (so they
           are constant expressions) that the lock, signal and unlock
           functions then accept without an init call.
test       t/010-initializers.c
nomutant   header content check; needs the Tier 0 header mutants

assertion  XBD.pthread.h.011
anchor     basedefs/pthread.h.html#DESCRIPTION/PTHREAD_ONCE_INIT
class      required
since      2001
says       A static pthread_once_t initialised with PTHREAD_ONCE_INIT
           makes two pthread_once() calls run the routine exactly once.
test       t/011-once-init.c
nomutant   header content check; needs the Tier 0 header mutants

assertion  XBD.pthread.h.012
anchor     basedefs/pthread.h.html#DESCRIPTION/PTHREAD_NULL
class      required
since      2024
says       PTHREAD_NULL initialises a static pthread_t and an automatic
           one, and compares equal to neither the calling thread's ID
           nor that of a running thread created by the test.
test       t/012-null-thread.c
nomutant   header content check; needs the Tier 0 header mutants

assertion  XBD.pthread.h.013
anchor     basedefs/pthread.h.html#DESCRIPTION/PTHREAD_BARRIER_SERIAL_THREAD
class      required
since      2001
says       PTHREAD_BARRIER_SERIAL_THREAD is nonzero and differs from
           EINVAL, the one error the pthread_barrier_wait() page names.
note       The page names no other error for the function (EBUSY is
           not one of its errors), so only EINVAL is compared.
test       t/013-serial-thread.c
nomutant   header content check; needs the Tier 0 header mutants
